<section class="bg-brand-paper px-6 py-16 md:py-24 section-rule">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[40fr_60fr] gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-start">

      <!-- Heading left -->
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-serif); font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,2.75rem); line-height:1.15; letter-spacing:0; font-weight:500; color:#111111; margin:0;">
          What's an Adult Family Home?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <!-- Body right -->
      <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:16px;">
        <p style="font-size:17px; color:rgba(17,17,17,0.72); line-height:1.65; margin:0;">
          An Adult Family Home is a licensed residential house where a small number of residents live and receive around-the-clock care. Washington State licenses and inspects AFHs under the same regulatory standards as larger facilities.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size:17px; color:rgba(17,17,17,0.72); line-height:1.65; margin:0;">
          The difference is scale. Fewer residents means caregivers know each person well, and daily life stays closer to what home actually feels like.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/about"
          style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; font-size:15px; font-weight:500; color:var(--color-brand-sage); margin-top:4px; text-decoration:none;"
          class="hover:text-brand-terra transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          Learn what makes an AFH different <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
